// The frame loop, the same shape as demos/gfxdemo/loop/mainloop.id: spin advances
// a tick counter until a frame reports the window wants to close, then tears
// the window down.

// `ok` is threaded into the loop's live flag rather than discarded: with no
// display glwin_open returns 0 and glwin_poll then returns -1 forever, so a loop
// that starts unconditionally never ends. Every windowed demo in this tree had
// that bug -- `DISPLAY= ./prog` ran until it was killed.
// Only the run <= 0 branch is cased: run > 0 only terminates through a real
// GFX_MAX_FRAMES-bounded present/poll cycle, which a case cannot set up --
// see main.id's note.
loop(int ok) {
  spin(ok, 0);
  glwin_close();
} return void;
given scene_initialize (0):() then mesh_state:("-1000,108,2631720,36")
given scene_initialize (-3):() then mesh_state:("-1000,108,2631720,36")

spin(int run, int tick) {
  while(run > 0) {
    int frame_event = frame(tick);
    run = inp_live(frame_event);
    tick = sys_next(tick);
  }
} return void;
